<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16460" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-ventĭlo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a., <i>to set in motion</i> (the air), <i>to
				fan</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(aërem graviorem) emendant assiduo
					linteorum jactatu eventilando,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 3, 28, § 49</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Just. 44, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>:
			frumenta, <i>to winnow</i>, i. e. <i>to
				purify by winnowing</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 6,
				23</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opes eventilatae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>scattered</i>, <i>dissipated</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
